Source package: xdg-desktop-portal-gtk

end-session-after-monitors-close.patch
    Lets the session end only once the applications which monitor it have quit. xdg-desktop-portal-gtk
    serves the Inhibit portal on GNOME, and is a client of gnome-session. When the session ends,
    gnome-session sends EndSession to its clients, and xdg-desktop-portal-gtk tells every application
    which monitors the session through the portal that it ends. GTK 4 applications and Chromium quit
    then, and Firefox with patches/firefox/quit-at-session-end.patch. xdg-desktop-portal-gtk answered
    EndSession at once, though, so gnome-session ended the session about 30 ms later, and systemd
    stopped the applications' scopes and GNOME Shell while the applications were still quitting. An
    application then lost its child processes in the middle of quitting, or GTK ended it when its
    Wayland connection broke.

    xdg-desktop-portal-gtk now answers EndSession only once every application which monitors the
    session has closed its inhibit session. The portal closes it also when the application
    disconnects from the bus, so also when it exits. xdg-desktop-portal-gtk answers after 8 seconds
    at most, as gnome-session waits 10 seconds for the answer, and logs every inhibit session still
    open as "The session ends with inhibit session ... still open". An application which monitors
    the session without quitting when it ends delays the end of the session by these 8 seconds.

    The wait is in wait_for_monitors_to_close in src/inhibit.c, which client_proxy_signal calls on
    EndSession, and inhibit_session_close ends it. After a version bump, check that EndSession is still
    answered there. The patch adds no test, as xdg-desktop-portal-gtk has no test suite. The session
    test in tests/session/ checks it with Firefox: logging out has to let Firefox quit before GNOME
    Shell shuts down. Not proposed upstream yet.

    Check by hand after a rebuild and a new login, with Firefox open:

      log out and in, then journalctl --user -b | grep -E 'app-gnome-firefox-.*scope|Shutting down GNOME Shell'
                              the scope of Firefox should end before GNOME Shell shuts down
